From: Sacha Gavino <sacha.gavino@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 19 Jul 2026 15:32:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] Write the dust distribution as raw state; add the
 sigma(a) reduction

src/dust/README.md requires a dust-mass and grain-number conservation
diagnostic before the first coagulation term is written. This is it.

New dust_distribution.out, written by write_current_dust at every output time
(created at index=1, appended after), one row per (time, bin):
  time[yr]  bin  radius[cm]  mass[g]  n_k[/H]  m_k*n_k[g/H]
plus three per-time running totals repeated on each row for easy loading:
  dust_mass[g/H] = sum_k m_k n_k, grain_number[/H] = sum_k n_k, dust_mass_sink.

- n_k is the total grain number of the bin summed over CHARGE STATES
  (GRAIN0_k + GRAIN0_k-). Grains move between charge states but are not
  created or destroyed, so the charge-state sum -- not the neutral abundance
  alone -- is the conserved per-bin number. The neutral abundance by itself
  drifts as grains charge and discharge.
- Written as raw state, deliberately not the mass-weighted sigma(a): that
  reduction is a python script, per project convention.
- The grain bins stay in abundances.out as well; they are state
  (abundances(INDGRAIN(k)) = n_k/n_H) and nothing is removed from there.

scripts/dust_distribution.py is the reduction: sigma(a) = m dn/dln a and the
n(a,t) view, plus the conservation table. dln a is computed per bin from
neighbours so it also handles a non-uniform tabulated grid.

Verified on the derived + MRN grid: sum_k m_k n_k equals
initial_dtg_mass_ratio * AMU exactly at t0 and drifts by at most 1.2e-14
relative across all output times (grain number 9.0e-15) -- floating-point
round-off from integrating the charge transfer, i.e. zero physical drift, which
is the acceptance criterion while the distribution is still static. The per-bin
m_k*n_k column sums to the dust_mass column to 1.2e-15. sigma(a) from the
reduction follows a^0.5, as MRN requires (m dn/dln a ~ a^3 a^-3.5 a = a^0.5),
and all output times overlap. tests/roundtrip_derived.sh still passes
byte-identical after these changes.
